      "line": 1,
      "start_column": 0,
      "end_column": 34,
      "quote": "# Museum accession activity viewer"
    },
    {
      "id": "S0002",
      "file": "README.md",
      "line": 3,
      "start_column": 0,
      "end_column": 75,
      "quote": "The activity panel reads a cached first batch and then incremental batches."
    },
    {
      "id": "S0003",
      "file": "README.md",
      "line": 4,
      "start_column": 0,
      "end_column": 80,
      "quote": "The host supplies rendering and history adapters. The pinned runtime and host ad"
    },
    {
      "id": "S0004",
      "file": "README.md",
      "line": 4,
      "start_column": 80,
      "end_column": 120,
      "quote": "apter are described in docs/host-api.md."
    },
    {
      "id": "S0005",
      "file": "README.md",
      "line": 6,
      "start_column": 0,
      "end_column": 78,
      "quote": "Public workspace methods are select(feed, mode) and hide(). Selecting the same"
    },
    {
      "id": "S0006",
      "file": "README.md",
      "line": 7,
      "start_column": 0,
      "end_column": 80,
      "quote": "feed after leaving creates a new panel visit. Changing selection or hiding stops"
    },
    {
      "id": "S0007",
      "file": "README.md",
      "line": 8,
      "start_column": 0,
      "end_column": 79,
      "quote": "the previous visit's visible output; the selected visit must keep receiving new"
    },
    {
      "id": "S0008",
      "file": "README.md",
      "line": 9,
      "start_column": 0,
      "end_column": 54,
      "quote": "batches. Reusing an existing feed object is supported."
    },
    {
      "id": "S0009",
      "file": "README.md",
      "line": 11,
      "start_column": 0,
      "end_column": 71,
      "quote": "paintRows(frame, navigation) commits rows for the current visit and may"
    },
    {
      "id": "S0010",
      "file": "README.md",
      "line": 12,
      "start_column": 0,
      "end_column": 76,
      "quote": "synchronously navigate or hide the panel. It can return a Promise for layout"
    },
    {
      "id": "S0011",
      "file": "README.md",
      "line": 13,
      "start_column": 0,
      "end_column": 76,
      "quote": "completion. The count belongs to those painted rows and becomes visible only"
    },
    {
      "id": "S0012",
      "file": "README.md",
      "line": 14,
      "start_column": 0,
      "end_column": 76,
      "quote": "after that paint has completed, if its visit is still current. Ordinary live"
    },
    {
      "id": "S0013",
      "file": "README.md",
      "line": 15,
      "start_column": 0,
      "end_column": 78,
      "quote": "counts remain required. A component or feed object can survive several visits."
    },
    {
      "id": "S0014",
      "file": "README.md",
      "line": 17,
      "start_column": 0,
      "end_column": 80,
      "quote": "History records each received batch once its decoding completes. A batch already"
    },
    {
      "id": "S0015",
      "file": "README.md",
      "line": 18,
      "start_column": 0,
      "end_column": 77,
      "quote": "accepted by the subscriber remains useful to history after leaving the panel;"
    },
    {
      "id": "S0016",
      "file": "README.md",
      "line": 19,
      "start_column": 0,
      "end_column": 80,
      "quote": "retiring a view does not revoke accepted history work. Removing a listener stops"
    },
    {
      "id": "S0017",
      "file": "README.md",
      "line": 20,
      "start_column": 0,
      "end_column": 78,
      "quote": "new reception, while already-started decoding and painting may still complete."
    },
    {
      "id": "S0018",
      "file": "README.md",
      "line": 22,
      "start_column": 0,
      "end_column": 78,
      "quote": "The independent metrics consumer intentionally ignores the cached snapshot and"
    },
    {
      "id": "S0019",
      "file": "README.md",
      "line": 23,
      "start_column": 0,
      "end_column": 74,
      "quote": "observes deltas. Its policy is outside this panel repair unless separately"
    },
    {
      "id": "S0020",
      "file": "README.md",
      "line": 24,
      "start_column": 0,
      "end_column": 75,
      "quote": "authorized. Preserve APIs, payloads, rendering timing and history behavior."
